      "text": "The vibrant intellectual centres of the Islamic world brought Greek thought and science to medieval Europe from the 12th century onwards. During this period, Zodiacal imagery began to appear, and the Zodiac emerged as a link to the seasons, a way of making sense of the movement of time, and, profoundly, as a symbolic bridge to the Divine.\n\nIn Chartres Cathedral, the Zodiac appears in stone and stained glass at least three times. Many other cathedrals from the late medieval period in France and elsewhere contain Zodiacal imagery. The planets and signs began to fill late medieval Books of Hours, illuminating the borders of manuscripts. \n\nThis illustrated lecture will examine how this archetypal symbolism continues to move through us. \n\n\ud83c\udf9f\ufe0f Comment \"SYMBOL\" to get more info about the lecture.\n\ud83d\udcc5 Wednesday 9 December 2026\n\ud83d\udd5b 18:30 - 20:00\n\ud83d\udccd King's Foundation School of Traditional Arts\n\ud83e\uddd1\u200d\ud83c\udfebLynn Bell @lynnbellparis",
